# The .gitignore is authoritative on the versioned / local boundary, and every entry
# says WHY it is ignored — a readable .gitignore prevents case-by-case judgement, by
# a human as much as by an agent.
#
# Nothing private is ignored here, because nothing private is here. This repository is
# public in full; what is private lives in sibling repositories, outside its tree. A
# boundary drawn by structure holds against a mistyped command; one drawn by a rule in
# this file only holds while the rule does.
